# M_PwReview_Neutral - the material you judge geometry under.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Every default material the engine hands an unbound mesh
# slot carries a grid TEXTURE: WorldGridMaterial, DefaultMaterial and M_Grid all
# do, and all three project it in WORLD space, so the pattern is fixed to the
# world and slides across the surface as the mesh moves. Over one session that
# texture was filed as a geometry defect twice - as "normal-interpolation
# faceting" on mobius_band (a computed 5.4 degree crease angle was quoted) and as
# a "corrugation from remesh_uniform, then from twist" on driftwood, which four
# successive authors chased through a six-column op probe that came back clean on
# every column. This material has no texture in it at all, so nothing it draws
# can be mistaken for something the mesh is doing.
#
# HOW TO INSTALL IT.
#
#   call("material.compile_mgir", { text: <this file>, save: true })
#   call("material.authoring.compile_material",
#        { assetPath: "/Game/PinWrightExamples/Materials/M_PwReview_Neutral" })
#
# WHY MID GREY AND NOT WHITE. 0.18 linear is the standard 18% grey card. White
# clips against any key light bright enough to model form, and a clipped surface
# hides exactly the shading gradient a review is reading. Everything is a
# parameter so one master serves the prop, the ground plane and any darker or
# lighter variant through material instances - do not compile a second master.
#
# ROUGHNESS 0.55, NOT 0.9. A fully matte surface has no specular gradient, and
# the specular gradient is what makes a curvature error visible. 0.55 keeps a
# broad highlight that rolls across a curve without turning into a mirror.

entry material `/Game/PinWrightExamples/Materials/M_PwReview_Neutral` {
    %base = call `/Script/Engine.MaterialExpressionVectorParameter`(ParameterName: "BaseColor", Group: "Review", SortPriority: 0, DefaultValue: [0.18, 0.18, 0.18, 1.0]) @(-600, -100)
    %roughness = call `/Script/Engine.MaterialExpressionScalarParameter`(ParameterName: "Roughness", Group: "Review", SortPriority: 16, DefaultValue: 0.55) @(-600, 120)
    %metallic = call `/Script/Engine.MaterialExpressionScalarParameter`(ParameterName: "Metallic", Group: "Review", SortPriority: 32, DefaultValue: 0.0) @(-600, 260)
    %specular = call `/Script/Engine.MaterialExpressionScalarParameter`(ParameterName: "Specular", Group: "Review", SortPriority: 48, DefaultValue: 0.5) @(-600, 400)

    output BaseColor: %base
    output Roughness: %roughness
    output Metallic: %metallic
    output Specular: %specular
}
